            <ArticleTitle>[Immunogenetic characteristics of patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The distribution of the principal erythrocyte and HLA-antigens was investigated in 202 males aged 20-50 years with a history of myocardial infarction and various courses of coronary heart disease. The occurrence of one or the other group of antigens differed both as compared with a group of healthy subjects (619 subjects) and in relation to the anamnestic and clinical characteristics of the disease course. The findings helped to draw a conclusion as to the presence of associative links between a number of the studied antigens (A (II), MN, HLA-B7, HLA-B14, HLA-B15, HLA-CW4) and the risk of the development of, at least, some forms of coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
